# On-Page SEO Rules — Warriors Defence Academy (2026)

Apply every applicable rule below whenever you generate or update any web content on this project.

---

## TARGET KEYWORDS (priority order)

### Homepage primary cluster
1. `best nda coaching in lucknow` — primary (GSC pos ~3.4)
2. `nda coaching in lucknow` — secondary
3. `best nda coaching` — secondary (also on India page)
4. Brand: `warriors defence academy`, `warriors defence academy fees`

### India landing (`/best-nda-coaching-in-india`)
1. `best nda coaching in india` — primary
2. `best nda coaching` — secondary
3. `top nda coaching` — secondary
4. `top nda coaching in india` — secondary

### Site-wide secondary
6. `ssb coaching in lucknow`, `cds coaching in lucknow`, `defence academy lucknow`, `nda exam date 2026`, `ssb oir`

### Keyword tracking sheet (required)
Whenever you assign or change target keywords for any page, update:
- `seo/keyword-map.csv`
- `seo/KEYWORD-MAP.md`

Record: page, path, primary keyword, secondary keywords, status, last_updated.
No two pages may share the same primary keyword.

---

## 1. TITLE TAGS

- Max **53–60 characters**
- Primary keyword in the **first 3 words**
- Formula: `[Primary Keyword] | [Brand Name]`
- Home page title: `Best NDA Coaching in Lucknow | Warriors Defence Academy`
- No duplicate titles across pages
- Include year modifier ("2026") only for time-sensitive content

## 2. META DESCRIPTIONS

- **120–160 characters** exactly (never exceed 160)
- Include primary keyword naturally
- End with a CTA: "Enroll now", "Apply today", "Call now"
- Home page description: `Best NDA coaching in Lucknow at Warriors Defence Academy — 50,000+ students, 5,000+ selections, India's largest GTO ground. Enroll now!`
- Every page must have a **unique** meta description

## 3. H1 HEADING (most critical on-page signal)

- **ONE H1 per page** — never more
- Must contain the primary keyword
- Home page H1: `Best NDA Coaching in` + highlight `Lucknow, India`
- Course pages: include exam name + "coaching" + Lucknow in H1/title when commercial
- Blog posts: include target keyword in H1; prefer GSC-winning topics (OIR, exam dates, badges, Agniveer)

## 4. HEADING HIERARCHY

```
H1: Primary keyword — one per page
  H2: Main sections (what users expect to find)
    H3: Sub-points, steps, FAQs, examples
```

- H2s answer the implied question of that section
- Include LSI/semantic keywords in H2s (synonyms, related terms)
- Never skip levels (H1 → H3 without H2)

## 5. KEYWORD PLACEMENT — place primary keyword in ALL of:

1. Title tag (first 3 words)
2. H1 heading
3. First 100 words of body content
4. At least one H2 subheading
5. URL slug
6. Image alt text (where image relates to the topic)
7. Meta description

**Density:** 1–2% natural usage. Never stuff keywords.

## 6. URL SLUGS

- Short, lowercase, hyphenated: `/courses/nda-coaching` ✅
- Keyword-rich, no stop words (a, the, of)
- No dates in evergreen content URLs

## 7. CONTENT QUALITY RULES

- Answer the page's target question in the **first 100–150 words**
- Include at least one of: stat, testimonial quote, or specific result
- E-E-A-T signals required: credentials, selection numbers, faculty bios
- Keep content updated — add "Last Updated" when refreshing
- Every sentence must add value — no padding

## 8. IMAGE OPTIMIZATION

- File names: descriptive + keyword, hyphenated (`nda-coaching-gto-ground-lucknow.webp`)
- Alt text: natural description + keyword (`alt="NDA coaching students at Warriors Defence Academy Lucknow"`)
- Format: **WebP** always (JPEG fallback for photos)
- Use `next/image` — never raw `<img>` tags
- Add `priority` prop to above-the-fold images (hero carousel first slide)

## 9. INTERNAL LINKING

- **3–5 internal links** per new page or post
- Anchor text must be descriptive keywords — never "click here"
- Link from high-traffic pages to important course/contact pages
- All important pages must be reachable within 3 clicks from homepage

## 10. SCHEMA MARKUP — use correct type per page

| Page | Schema Type |
|---|---|
| Homepage | Full `@graph` — see `lib/seo.ts buildHomeSchemaGraph()` |
| Course pages | `Course` + `EducationalOrganization` |
| Blog / articles | `Article` or `BlogPosting` |
| FAQ sections | `FAQPage` |
| Contact / location | `LocalBusiness` + `PostalAddress` |
| Any page | `BreadcrumbList` |

- Homepage schema is already built in `buildHomeSchemaGraph()` — do not simplify it
- Add `FAQPage` schema whenever there is a visible FAQ section

## 11. SITE-SPECIFIC DEFAULTS

When writing any content for Warriors Defence Academy always include:

- **Academy name:** Warriors Defence Academy (not "WDA" in body copy)
- **Location:** Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh (not just "Lucknow" for pan-India content)
- **Phone:** +91 94522 45729 (primary), +91 70810 11964 (secondary)
- **Address:** 545-Ga/1 Chha, Near Kapoorthala Chauraha, Beside Raidas Railway Crossing, Lucknow - 226024
- **Key stats to use:** 50,000+ students trained, 5,000+ selections, 200+ expert mentors, 15+ years, AIR #1 multiple years
- **USP phrases:** "India's largest GTO ground", "retired military officers", "India's best NDA coaching"

## 12. CORE WEB VITALS — never degrade these

- Always use `next/image` (auto-optimised)
- Add `priority` on LCP image (hero carousel slide 1)
- No layout shift from dynamic content — use skeleton loaders
- Avoid render-blocking scripts in `<head>`

## 13. AI SEARCH / FEATURED SNIPPETS

- Answer questions directly in the **first sentence** under each heading
- Use numbered lists for processes, bullet lists for features
- Include exact question phrases as H2/H3 headings
- Add specific numbers and dates — AI engines prefer citable facts

